{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/561137-wayward-ghoul","id":561137,"title":"Wayward Ghoul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-19T13:52:48-07:00","id":561137,"title":"Wayward Ghoul","content":"I had a random idea when re-reading the section on ghouls in 2e. It's not something I'd use in a game, except maybe as an NPC mcguffin for a story. It's mostly meant to be a thought experiment, so I don't really expect there will be a one true answer. If there is, though, cool! I like insights into the metaphysics of WoD.<br /> <br /> So say there is a ghoul. Their regnant is secretive enough that the vampire population in the city doesn't know the ghoul exists. As far as I know, there's no way to detect a ghoul other than the whole unaging/able to use vampire powers thing.<br /> <br /> Say their regnant dies. The ghoul is fully bonded to said regnant, and so has essentially a year of bond-free feeding ahead of them.<br /> <br /> Say their regnant knew most of the havens of other vampires, and now the ghoul can feed from the various vampires of the city while they sleep during the day. A different one every single night.<br /> <br /> Now, the text clearly states that the regnant is usually the one that ghouled the ghoul. This suggests that it isn't always the case. This would also suggest that a ghoul can switch regnants over time for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Who would count as their regnant for the purposes of... well, everything that a regnant does with this feeding schedule? Disciplines. Clan-ghoul merits. Blood sympathy, if they have that merit. Would the constant influx of Vitae from many different clans have any adverse/beneficial effects? How would you run this in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:08:57-07:00","id":561195,"title":"","content":"I might allow them to purchase multiple merits based upon having different regnants, or use Sanctity of Merits on the things that are no longer applicable with a new Regnant. They might also acquire or sort of create some kind of merit reflecting a resistance to blood bonding by other vampires.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of the Alley Men in a way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T18:58:38-07:00","id":561475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/561137-wayward-ghoul#post561137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would count as their regnant for the purposes of... well, everything that a regnant does with this feeding schedule? Disciplines. Clan-ghoul merits. Blood sympathy, if they have that merit. Would the constant influx of Vitae from many different clans have any adverse/beneficial effects? How would you run this in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div> Regnant is usually the one with the blood bond controlling the ghoul. The one who's the dominant in the relationship. <br /> <br /> For everything else? Its the one who ghouled them. In a way, ghouls are like half-vampires. All that matters is who originally &quot;infected&quot; them. Their original clan comes from that, the blood sympathy, the affinities, bloodlines, and more. <br /> <br /> Think of it this way - the regnant is like the covenant that the ghoul belongs to, while clan is made at that first taste of vitae with the will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T03:40:52-07:00","id":561761,"title":"","content":"Doesn't a blood bond break immediately if the regnant dies? That was definitely how it worked in first edition...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T03:59:31-07:00","id":561765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/561137-wayward-ghoul?p=561761#post561761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't a blood bond break immediately if the regnant dies? That was definitely how it worked in first edition...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any rule to that effect. The year wait, the Ordo scale are the only listed 2e methods; some may include acieving a third tier bond destroying smaller bonds count too. But death is not listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T04:48:35-07:00","id":561789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/561137-wayward-ghoul?p=561475#post561475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Regnant is usually the one with the blood bond controlling the ghoul. The one who's the dominant in the relationship.<br /> <br /> For everything else? Its the one who ghouled them. In a way, ghouls are like half-vampires. All that matters is who originally &quot;infected&quot; them. Their original clan comes from that, the blood sympathy, the affinities, bloodlines, and more.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way - the regnant is like the covenant that the ghoul belongs to, while clan is made at that first taste of vitae with the will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think I would personally interpret it this way. After all, it says that the regnant doesn't need to be the one that turned the mortal into a ghoul, and the merits use the same terminology, &quot;regnant,&quot; for merit prerequisites. That said, I can see this interpretation as there being two meanings for 'regnant,' and it's certainly an interpretation with interesting consequences. The one that comes foremost to mind is; if a ghoul has a Clan from the moment they are ghouled, would you implement any kind of special case or consequences for one getting embraced by a different Clan? Say, Ghouled by a Ventrue then stolen and Embraced by, say, a Gangrel or a Mekhet? Or would the new Clan just overwrite the old, with the exception of whatever Disciplines the Ghoul learned from their Regnant?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/561137-wayward-ghoul?p=561195#post561195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might allow them to purchase multiple merits based upon having different regnants, or use Sanctity of Merits on the things that are no longer applicable with a new Regnant. They might also acquire or sort of create some kind of merit reflecting a resistance to blood bonding by other vampires.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of the Alley Men in a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sanctity of Merits thing is probably the most mechanically sound and least prone to abuse. The fact that it's a bit prone to abuse is precisely why I clarified that this isn't for a PC. So it's a good method in that regard, I think. There's a ghoul merit that makes blood bonds less potent on them, but none that make it so they can resist (I don't think they can even resist at all like vampires can by default), so that might be an interesting way to go, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:54:25-07:00","id":566284,"title":"","content":"In my opinion the ghoul is linked to their original regnant (i.e. the vampire who bestowed the ghoul status onto the ghoul via willpower expenditure) similiar to the process of siring.<br /> But in case of the wayward ghoul i can imgaine if a new regnant &quot;invests&quot; again into the ghoul, she will switch her parrent clan. <br /> <br /> just drinking vitae - does not normally give you a link to a clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:14:09-07:00","id":566289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/561137-wayward-ghoul?p=561789#post561789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I would personally interpret it this way. After all, it says that the regnant doesn't need to be the one that turned the mortal into a ghoul, and the merits use the same terminology, &quot;regnant,&quot; for merit prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div> To each their own. I think the merits were written under the assumption that the first to ghoul is the same as the dominant vampire in control- ghouls usually don't switch masters, that's a niche case. <br /> <br /> Well, I'm basing my thoughts off 1e rules, so things may changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I can see this interpretation as there being two meanings for 'regnant,' and it's certainly an interpretation with interesting consequences. The one that comes foremost to mind is; if a ghoul has a Clan from the moment they are ghouled, would you implement any kind of special case or consequences for one getting embraced by a different Clan? Say, Ghouled by a Ventrue then stolen and Embraced by, say, a Gangrel or a Mekhet? Or would the new Clan just overwrite the old, with the exception of whatever Disciplines the Ghoul learned from their Regnant? </div> </div> </div> I'm going by 1e here, but no, there's never been a penalty for being a ghoul of one clan, then being fully Embraced by another. Yes, the Embrace completely and utterly overwrites anything from the ghoul, save disciplines learned. Yes, this means that, in theory, a ghoul PC can learn different clan powers, then become a vamp and get different affinities, but I think the threat of such gaming of the system is minimal. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:15:58-07:00","id":566290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/561137-wayward-ghoul?p=566289#post566289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, this means that, in theory, a ghoul PC can learn different clan powers, then become a vamp and get different affinities, but I think the threat of such gaming of the system is minimal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if it happens in-game, that's just character development. At CC, it's as good a justification as any for spending one of your initial Discipline dots on an Out-Of-Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}